\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. We bless Thee, Lord, for all this common life
\par Can give of rest and joy amidst its strife;
\par For earth and trees and sea and clouds and springs;
\par For work, and all the lessons that it brings;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For Pisgah gleams of newer, fairer truth,
\par Which ever ripening still renews our youth;
\par For fellowship with noble souls and wise,
\par Whose hearts beat time to music of the skies;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For each achievement human toil can reach;
\par For all that patriots win, and poets teach;
\par For the old light that that gleams on history's page
\par For the new hope that shines on each new age.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. May we to these our lights be ever true,
\par Find hope and strength and joy for ever new,
\par To heavenly visions still obedient prove,
\par The eternal Law, writ by the Almighty Love!
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

